From c93237e4696767a7b919dcf92c094df4ea1cbf48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:22:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 232/298] Part views: fast hidden-line projection, section,
 zoom, up vector, time limit

projectVisible clipped every face against every face whose box overlapped it, on
one thread.  Now a 2048 px depth buffer picks the occluders (the groups on top
over the face, plus the other triangles of their curved face), faces and edges run
on all cores, tessellation too, and shapes made only of planar triangles (STL via
makeShapeFromMesh) go the mesh way: coplanar triangles merge and no lines are drawn
between them, and BRepMesh is skipped.  Results are the same as before (visible
area within 0.001 %), 1200 parts 17.7 s -> 3.9 s, 300 STL-derived parts 48 s -> 1.5 s.

New keywords for renderImage / projectVisible / exportSvg / exportPptx: up,
region / focus (zoom), section=(point, normal) with filled and hatched cut faces,
sectionColor, hatch, progress (stderr), maxSeconds / timeout (partial result,
nearest faces first, RuntimeWarning, 'complete': False), threads.  Named views
iso-front-left, iso-back-right, iso-bottom and its variants.  Command line:
--up, --region, --focus, --section (z=10, -x=5 or px,py,pz,nx,ny,nz),
--deflection, --max-seconds, --progress.

Coincident faces in the CPU renderer no longer flicker pixel by pixel into solid
black.  "No such file" after a script hints at 'script.py -- value'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
